usiness everybody is to his best  in order to win the support from the  different  carrier we can benefit from the one bear  world  initiative but another financial support  for sure  what we get is because the one bear  worldwide initiative will create more  trade opportunities  and this trade opportunity as a carrier  and as a terminal  we will benefit from that chinese  investment has supercharged pereira's  port but china's clout  has also raised concerns that local  businesses  could be squeezed out almost all the  companies in greece are small medium  enterprises  they listen to the fear  they're afraid that these huge companies  will take their business from their  hands business groups say initial  antagonism  has largely turned to acceptance and the  hunt for opportunity  there are a lot of people that they are  not satisfied because  they thought we could also exploit the  sport by ourselves  of course there are some people that  blame chinese that they took advantage  of the greek crisis but on the other  hand we very  well know that the rules of business is  that  when you find an investment in good  price you go for it  it's a catalyst it's an opportunity for  all of us to  start negotiating how we invest  paired with support the supply chain and  logistics  are hinderland and hitherland is where  we can invest  where we can take advantage where we can  use  tools like creating clusters  like creating growth of volumes  in order to produce wealth but the  belton road fueled push of chinese firms  across europe  has also stoked fears about china's  so-called soft power reach  and geopolitical ambitions chinese  state-owned firms now control  around 10 of europe's container terminal  capacity according to the international  transport forum  the european commission says it welcomes  the belton road initiative  but with caveats there are two  major issues which we want to make sure  that that happens all those projects  financed by china  and the others should be economically  and  environmentally sustainable and the  second especially course for  tender should be competitive and open  for everybody  we want to be part of this project  but all the concrete investments  must be reasonable and there are other  concerns beyond simply  how investments are implemented  the european union in particular is very  concerned about  china trying to divide  and conquer europe through the belton  road there are countries in  central south eastern  europe that are leaning forward because  they haven't recovered from the global  financial crisis as other countries have  and they really want to take advantage  of these  chinese offers for assistance and  infrastructure development  and so it's those countries many of  those countries that we see  are susceptible to receiving the  benefits of the belton road  and then turning around and  basically taking steps and actions that  support china  in other venues and in political fora  and that's where i think  european leaders are growing concern in  areas uh  where you need unanimity voting inside  the eu  and which are sensitive the chinese just  need to own so to speak one government  out of 28 to block uh common resolutions  on an in a number of areas what do you  say to those  people who are concerned that aligning  yourself so closely  with chinese state-owned companies like  costco  creates a dependency for a country like  greece for greece  in greece as greek we need investments  we need foreign investments if these  investments they have come from china  they are mostly welcome for me if they  could come from germany it would be also  very welcome  or united states  [Music]  coming up we go to germany where the ceo  of siemens tells us  why he thinks ignoring the belton road  is more of a risk  than getting on board and if you have an  initiative  good or bad right or wrong well  perceived or not which covers 70  of the global population you better take  that seriously  [Music]  